F3: soilworks(ash→soil), greenhouse(soil+water→food), mine→ore, forge(ore+power→metal); cap() enforced + overflow logged in endTurn step 2. Score 2.

F4: colonist records {skill,fatigue,morale,job,assigned}; outputMult() reads c.skill/c.fatigue for production. Score 2.

F5: needF/needW consumption, shortF/shortW→morale-10/-12, outputMult reads c.morale; morale+2 on no-shortage turn (recoverable). Score 2.

F6: 10 RESEARCH nodes, pre.every() prereq check, cost deducted in doResearch, each flag read in outputMult/cap/needs/price. Score 2.

F7: 12 EVENTS, weighted pool.reduce/roll selection, 5 events w/ 2-3 choices with distinct state effects, eventCd cooldown map. Score 2.

F8: price() uses stockF from S.res[g]/cap and S.drift[g] (random-walked each turn); trade() both buy/sell paths, caravan.inv[g] decremented/checked. Score 2.

F9: storm every 8 turns, sev scales with turn, t.damaged skips production entirely, stormwalls/windbreak reduce chance, repair() costs 2 parts+engineer. Score 2.

F10: serialize()=JSON.stringify(full state), validateLoad() checks required fields/shapes, saveerr shows parse/shape errors. Score 2.

F11: win (turn>60,pop≥12,food&water>0) and lose (col.length===0) both reachable, score() combines pop/research/stock/turn/win, renderOver() modal summary. Score 2.

F12: switchTab()/TABS wiring, renderLog() prefixes "T"+l.t, resTip()/data-tt tooltips explain formulas, keydown handler for Space/1-6, @media(max-width:420px) layout. Score 2.

F13: runTests() asserts prereqs/caps/determinism/save-load roundtrip/roster integrity (not trivial); runBenchmark() runs greedyStep loop headless, hashState() printed. Score 2.

G1: RESEARCH flag (e.g. "filtration") read in outputMult() multiplying condenser output every production tick. Score 4.

G2: needF/needW shortfall sets shortF/shortW → c.morale-=10/-12 → outputMult() reads c.morale for ×0.6/×0.85 output penalty. Score 4.

G3: storm sets t.damaged=true → production loop `if(t.damaged)continue` (zero output) → repair() spends 2 parts+engineer, clears t.damaged, restoring next-turn output. Score 4.

G4: price() = BASEPRICE×S.drift[g](turn-drifting)×stockF(S.res[g]/cap), read in trade() both directions. Score 4.

G5: refugees choice branches call addColonist()/mutate res+morale differently; sickness choice mutates scrip vs colonist fatigue/assignment — all write to state, not just log. Score 4.

